'<!-- Single point force $F$ at distance $a$ from the left support, with reactions $V_A = F (l - a) / l$, $V_B = -F a / l$ and the bending peak $M_{max} = F (l - a) a / l$ at the load. -->
'<div style = "max-width:180mm;">
'<img style="width:190pt;" alt = "simply-supported-beam-concentrated-force.png" class="side" src = "../../Images/mechanics/beams/simply-supported-beam-concentrated-force.png">
'<p><b>Input data</b></p>
#UI 'Beam length -'l = 5m
#UI 'Load -'F = 10kN
#UI 'Distance -'a = 2m
#post
'<p><b>Internal forces</b></p>
'Bending
M_max = F*(l - a)*a/l|kNm
'Shear
V_A = F*(l - a)/l|kN
V_B = -F*a/l|kN
'<p><b>Diagrams</b></p>
#hide
PlotWidth = 600
PlotHeight = 150
#end hide
#end post
#UI 'Calculate internal forces at'x_1 = 1m
#post
'Bending
M(x) = V_A*x - F*(x - a)*(x > a)
$Plot{-M(x) @ x = 0m : l}
M(x_1)|kNm
'Shear
V(x) = V_A - F*(x > a)
$Plot{V(x) @ x = 0m : l}
V(x_1)|kN
#end post
'</div>
